// Arc: the code cracked, then read by hand. Hero: a page of Marshall Nirenberg's lab notebook (PD).
// Sims: the sequence archetype (sims/sequence.ts), filled with data only; every RNA, chain and
// effect on screen is computed from the letters. Cases read two real human genes, letters copied
// from NCBI RefSeq (pinned as public-domain texts) and numbered from the A of the start codon, as
// HGVS does: HBB variants named in dbSNP (c.27dup, the "codons 8/9 +G" frameshift, among them) and
// HBA2 c.427T>C. ABO c.261delG was the first case until a review showed a frame-blind scan wins it
// (in that GC-rich gene the next stop letters after the deletion happen to sit in the new frame);
// its sources stay pinned in the generated block below, cited by nothing.
